    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPT-5.6 Sol on levin-2023-goals-19: not-empirically-resolvable, resolvability 0.32";
    dc:description "Comparative cell biology can test continuity of particular pathways or behaviours, but the claim as stated packages those observations into a broad cognitive historical interpretation. Plausible outcomes remain compatible with non-cognitive descriptions, so it lacks a decisive empirical criterion.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: No observation uniquely distinguishes retention and scaling of an ancestral 'cognitive repertoire' from evolution of multicellular regulatory mechanisms unless specific ancestral capacities, homologous mechanisms, and quantitative collective goals are defined.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Ancestral states are not directly observed.", "Cognitive repertoire and anatomical goals are framework-dependent.", "Mechanistic continuity does not distinguish retention from exaptation.";
